---
// /history/research-map-2026-08-03 — THE PRESERVED RESEARCH MAP.
//
// WHY IT LIVES HERE NOW (Huayin, 2026-08-25). The governing principle: current reality owns the
// primary addresses; historical reality gets permanent, explicit historical addresses. A page being
// frozen is a reason to preserve it faithfully — it is not a reason for a frozen worldview to keep
// occupying the route a reader reasonably expects to describe the present. This map was written on
// 3 August 2026, is byte-frozen, and says in the present tense that The Theory of Data is at Version
// 4.0. It is at v6.1. So the map moves to an address that says what it is, and /research becomes the
// live estate.
//
// THE BYTES DO NOT MOVE AND ARE NOT EDITED. The same corpus file is imported. Ruling 8 (2026-08-21)
// demoted this file from publication authority and ruled explicitly against rewriting it;
// reconciliation row `rc-research-corpus-map-not-authority` records that its statements are
// "accurate as of its own edition date and not maintained against the record". Nothing about that
// changes here — only the address, and the chrome that frames it.
//
// THE CHROME IS THE ONLY THING THAT CHANGED. The orientation line and the closing block are authored
// in this file, never in the frozen markdown (verified: the corpus source contains neither string).
// They now say what the page is: a preserved historical record, the state it represents, that it is
// not maintained, and where current Research lives.
//
// THE EDITION THIS PAGE CAN TRUTHFULLY NAME IS v0.3, NOT v0.2. The filename says `v0_2` and the
// registry, the ledger and Ruling 8 all refer to it by that path — but the filename is stale, frozen
// at creation. The body has declared **v0.3** since f27318d. The filename is not renamed: it is the
// registry's key for a frozen consumer. THE ROUTE IS DATED, NOT VERSIONED, because those two markers
// disagree and the date is the one unambiguous fact.
//
// NO PUBLICATION FACTS ARE AUTHORED HERE. No DOI, version or date of any deposit is typed into this
// file, so this route states no publication fact — the ownership boundary settled in Unit 2.
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { Content } from '../../content/corpus/research_corpus_map_v0_2.md';

// Declared by the snapshot itself (line 5 of the source); the day comes from repo history.
const SNAPSHOT_EDITION = 'v0.3';
const SNAPSHOT_DECLARED_DATE = 'August 2026';
const SNAPSHOT_PRESERVED_SINCE = '3 August 2026';
---
<BaseLayout title="The research map, 3 August 2026 — a preserved record — datumwise"
  description="The datumwise research corpus map as it was written on 3 August 2026. A preserved historical record, kept exactly as written and not maintained as current. The current research estate is at /research."
  chip={false}>
  <div class="page-head">
    <p class="kicker">Historical record · the state of 3 August 2026</p>
    <p class="orientation">
      This is a <strong>preserved historical record</strong>. It keeps the research corpus map
      exactly as it was written on 3 August 2026, and it is <strong>not maintained as current</strong>
      — several of the documents it describes have been published in newer editions since, and the
      map goes on describing the ones it knew. The current research and source estate is at
      <a href="/research">Research</a>.
    </p>
  </div>

  <article class="prose research">
    <Content />
  </article>

  <p class="evidence-note">
    <strong>This record.</strong> This page renders the research map as it was at
    <strong>{SNAPSHOT_EDITION}</strong>, dated <strong>{SNAPSHOT_DECLARED_DATE}</strong> by the map
    itself and unchanged in this repository since {SNAPSHOT_PRESERVED_SINCE}. The text is preserved
    as written, not updated: the versions, dates and DOIs it names were accurate to that state and
    are not maintained as pointers to whatever is current, so some of them now name superseded
    editions. That is what makes it a record rather than an index. For the estate as it is now, see
    <a href="/research">Research</a>; publication truth is owned by the publication registry.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page-head { width: min(100% - 3rem, var(--measure)); margin: 0 auto; }
  .kicker { color: var(--ink-faint); }
  .orientation { margin-top: 0.6rem; font-size: 0.95rem; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .evidence-note { width: min(100% - 3rem, var(--measure)); margin: 3rem auto 0; padding-top: 1.5rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); font-size: 0.9rem; color: var(--ink-soft); }
</style>
